---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Privacy Policy — Vivobody";
const description =
  "Vivobody stores your training data on your device and sends nothing to the developer automatically.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} currentPath="/privacy/" bodyClass="legal-page">
  <article class="legal-article page-width">
    <header class="legal-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span></span> Privacy, plainly</p>
      <h1>Your training stays<br /><em>on your iPhone.</em></h1>
      <p class="legal-meta">Vivobody privacy policy · Effective August 7, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section class="legal-summary" aria-label="Privacy summary">
      <p>
        <strong>The short version:</strong> Your training stays on your device.
        There are no accounts, analytics, ads, or tracking, and Vivobody sends
        nothing to us automatically. Finished workouts go to Apple Health only
        if you enable it. A support email is sent only if you choose to send it.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>0</strong><span>accounts</span></li>
        <li><strong>0</strong><span>trackers</span></li>
        <li><strong>0</strong><span>automatic uploads</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <div class="legal-content">
      <section>
        <h2>Data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          Vivobody does not automatically collect or transmit data. We cannot
          see your workouts, your body weight, or anything else you enter in the
          app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contacting support</h2>
        <p>
          Contacting support is optional. When you tap Contact &amp; Support,
          Vivobody creates an editable email draft addressed to us. Along with
          anything you write, the draft includes the Vivobody version and build
          number, your iOS version, and your device model. This information is
          created on your device. No support message or diagnostic information
          is sent unless you tap Send. If you send the email, we use it only to
          respond and troubleshoot, and you may ask us to delete the conversation
          at any time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Where your data lives</h2>
        <p>
          Workouts, templates, exercise catalog edits, body weight entries, and
          settings are stored locally on your device in the app’s private
          database. Widget data is a small local snapshot shared between the app
          and its widgets through Apple’s App Group container, also entirely on
          your device. If you use iCloud device backups, your Vivobody data is
          included in your own encrypted backup, which we have no access to.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Apple Health</h2>
        <p>
          Saving workouts to Apple Health is optional and off by default. If you
          turn it on, Vivobody asks for <em>write-only</em> permission and saves
          each finished workout to the Health app. Vivobody never reads any data
          from Apple Health, and your health data is never transmitted anywhere
          by Vivobody. You can revoke access at any time in Settings &gt; Privacy
          &amp; Security &gt; Health, and manage or delete saved workouts in the
          Health app.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Purchases</h2>
        <p>
          Vivobody Pro is a one-time purchase processed entirely by Apple
          through the App Store. We never see your payment details. Purchase
          verification happens on your device using Apple’s StoreKit; no
          purchase information is sent to us.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Notifications</h2>
        <p>
          Rest timer alerts use local notifications scheduled on your device. No
          push notification service is used.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Siri, Spotlight, and widgets</h2>
        <p>
          Shortcuts, Spotlight search entries, and widget content are generated
          and stored on your device by Apple’s system frameworks. They are not
          shared with us or any third party.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          The Vivobody app contains no third-party SDKs, analytics frameworks,
          or advertising. If you choose to contact support, the message is sent
          through your email service to ours.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
        <p>
          Deleting the app deletes all Vivobody data from your device. Workouts
          previously saved to Apple Health remain in the Health app until you
          remove them there.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>
          Vivobody is not directed at children under 13 and does not
          automatically collect data from anyone, including children.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this
          address with a new effective date. Since the app sends nothing to us
          automatically, changes are expected to be rare.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy? Email
          {" "}<a href="mailto:vivobodyapp@gmail.com">vivobodyapp@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
